					zh: "目前就讀國立臺灣大學牙醫學系三年級，高中就讀彰化高中科學班。受科學班課程規劃影響，我於高二開始接觸科學研究，因對物理與生物感興趣，進入中興大學生物力學實驗室，研究蚤蠅的高頻率間歇性運動。進入大學後，我因研究導論課接觸牙周幹細胞，並結合自身十字韌帶受傷的經驗，開始思考牙周幹細胞應用於韌帶修復的可能性，也由此踏上新的研究歷程。",
					en: "I am currently a third-year student in the Department of Dentistry at National Taiwan University, and attended the Science Class at Changhua Senior High School. Shaped by the Science Class curriculum, I began scientific research in my second year of high school; out of interest in physics and biology, I joined a biomechanics laboratory at National Chung Hsing University to study the high-frequency intermittent locomotion of phorid flies. At university, an introductory research course introduced me to periodontal stem cells; combined with my own experience of a cruciate ligament injury, I began to consider whether periodontal stem cells could be applied to ligament repair, and so started a new research journey."
				},
				photo: "/speaker-xu-hezhen.jpg"
			},
