					en: "The Unexpected Diversity of Claw-only Attachment: A Mechanical Analysis of Termite Claw Morphology, Attachment Force and Ecological Adaptation"
				},
				bio: {
					zh: "目前就讀陽明交通大學百川學程。高中時因為對物理與生物的興趣而投入生物力學研究，從白蟻在不同粗糙表面的抓附表現出發，延伸到物種、形態與行為等方面。進入百川不分系後，我仍持續投入科學研究，同時開始接觸程式軟體設計，在跨領域的環境中慢慢形塑自己的未來走向。對我而言，基礎科學不只是高中階段的研究，更是促使我持續探索興趣與增進能力、結合不同領域的起點。",
					en: "I am currently enrolled in the Bai-Chuan Program (an undeclared-major program) at National Yang Ming Chiao Tung University. In high school, my interest in physics and biology led me into biomechanics research; starting from how termites grip rough surfaces of different kinds, I extended the work to species, morphology and behavior. After entering the Bai-Chuan program, I kept doing scientific research while also starting to study software design, gradually shaping my future direction in an interdisciplinary environment. For me, basic science is not just high school research but the starting point that keeps me exploring my interests, building my abilities and combining different fields."
				},
				photo: "/speaker-zhang-yuen.jpg"
			}
		]
